  "title": "The spread of modern democracy",
  "summary": "France's 1789 Declaration of the Rights of Man held that all sovereignty resides essentially in the nation. The Universal Declaration of Human Rights later stated that the will of the people shall be the basis of the authority of government. Today the United Nations calls democracy a core value, and supports it through human rights, development and peace and security.",
